# Git Commit with AI Messages

Always use the `aicommit` MCP server when committing changes instead of regular `git commit`.

## MCP Tools Available

- `commit_with_ai_message`: Generate AI commit message and commit immediately
- `generate_commit_message`: Generate message without committing (for preview)

## Usage

When the user asks to commit changes or when you need to commit:

```typescript
// Use the aicommit MCP tool
CallMcpTool({
  server: "aicommit",
  toolName: "commit_with_ai_message",
  arguments: {
    repo_path: "/path/to/repo",
    provider: "openrouter",  // or "gemini"
    include_context: false,   // set true to include previous commit
    retry_forever: false      // set true to retry on errors
  }
})
```

## Default Behavior

- Always use `commit_with_ai_message` for commits (not `git commit`)
- Use `repo_path: "."` when committing in the current repo
- Default provider is `openrouter` (can be changed if requested)
- Include context (`include_context: true`) only if explicitly requested

## Preview Before Committing

If the user wants to see the message first:

```typescript
CallMcpTool({
  server: "aicommit",
  toolName: "generate_commit_message",
  arguments: { repo_path: "." }
})
```

Then ask for approval before using `commit_with_ai_message`.
